    \node[anchor=west,font=\scriptsize] at (3.05*\j+0.55,-3.5) {\lab};}
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption[One rule over two texts]{The same alphabet, the same pairing and the same rule,
over deposited protein structures and over a compiled executable, shown as proportions
because the two corpora are nothing like the same size. The distributions differ and
should: compiled code is mostly small leaf functions that neither branch nor merge,
which is the null reading, while a protein kept by selection is under pressure to come
